      "message": "local run of sashiko says\n\n\u003e Could this signedness cast bypass the VMA boundary limits for file offsets near 8TB on 32-bit systems?\n\u003e\n\u003e On 32-bit architectures, pgoff_t is an unsigned long supporting file offsets up to 16TB. If a VMA is mapped at or near the 8TB boundary (vm_pgoff \u003e\u003d 0x80000000), casting it to a signed 32-bit long yields a negative\nvalue.\n\u003e\n\u003e If a fault occurs in the first few pages of this VMA, vmf-\u003epgoff - ra-\u003era_pages / 2 can evaluate to a positive value (e.g., 0x7FFFFFF8). The max_t macro will incorrectly identify the positive value as the maximum, assigning an offset preceding the VMA start.",
